## Design Patterns

### Repository Pattern
- **Interface** in `domain/repositories/` — defines the contract.
- **Implementation** in `data/repositories/` — handles API calls, caching, mapping.
- Wired together in State layer via Riverpod provider.

```dart
// domain/repositories/camera_repository.dart
abstract class CameraRepository {
  Future<List<Camera>> getCameras();
  Future<Camera> getCameraById(String id);
}

// data/repositories/camera_repository_impl.dart
class CameraRepositoryImpl implements CameraRepository {
  final CameraRemoteDataSource _remote;
  final CameraLocalDataSource _local;
  // ...
}

// state/cameras/camera_providers.dart
final cameraRepositoryProvider = Provider<CameraRepository>((ref) {
  return CameraRepositoryImpl(
    ref.watch(cameraRemoteDataSourceProvider),
    ref.watch(cameraLocalDataSourceProvider),
  );
});
```

### Use Case Pattern
- One public `call()` method per use case.
- Encapsulates a single business operation.
- Located in `domain/usecases/`.

```dart
class GetActiveCameras {
  final CameraRepository _repository;

  GetActiveCameras(this._repository);

  Future<List<Camera>> call() async {
    final cameras = await _repository.getCameras();
    return cameras.where((c) => c.status == CameraStatus.active).toList();
  }
}
```

### ViewModel Pattern
- Located in `presentation/viewmodels/`.
- Transforms domain entities into display-ready data.
- Contains UI-specific logic (formatting, sorting, filtering for display).

## File Naming Conventions

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Entity | `{name}.dart` | `camera.dart` |
| DTO | `{name}_dto.dart` | `camera_dto.dart` |
| Mapper | `{name}_mapper.dart` | `camera_mapper.dart` |
| Repository Interface | `{name}_repository.dart` | `camera_repository.dart` |
| Repository Impl | `{name}_repository_impl.dart` | `camera_repository_impl.dart` |
| Use Case | `{verb}_{noun}.dart` | `get_active_cameras.dart` |
| Provider | `{feature}_providers.dart` | `camera_providers.dart` |
| Notifier | `{feature}_notifier.dart` | `camera_list_notifier.dart` |
| Page | `{feature}_page.dart` | `camera_list_page.dart` |
| Widget | `zy_{name}.dart` | `zy_button.dart` |
| Test | `{file}_test.dart` | `camera_repository_impl_test.dart` |

## Rules

- NEVER create God classes. Each class has a single responsibility.
- NEVER skip the mapper step — DTOs and entities are always separate.
- ALWAYS create a use case for non-trivial business logic, even if it wraps a single repository call (enables future composition).
- ALWAYS keep the Domain layer free of Flutter imports — pure Dart only.
- ALWAYS group files by feature within each layer when the feature grows beyond 3 files.
